        <p>Step POLICE RETURNS. th„_ ,riZth fore. ooDaceinb,r 315t,1894, 54. all told, being no vacancies. The variations are, 1 re- Orel to improve his position and 1 dismissed for taluter,lness. The force therefore has been well sus- ther— unring the year ; it has been also well conducted, lz! being less reports against the men than in any sivlOus year. Leave of absence granted to all ranks. (1 clan ; sick leave 435 days; and hurt upon duty, 4 aYs. Nu ST. JOHN'S AMBULANCE CLASS. tbber holding certificates, sine chief constable, four 14, pesters, six sergeants, and 29 constables ; total, 40. ssafStajd. has hen given in 45 cases. The police force las: 'nsPected by Sir Herbert Croft,Bart.,on March 28th the' and I have reason to believe he was satisfied with tesult, but condemned the building.</p>
