        <p>WARRINGTON FREE CHURCH . Cu1:1 OIL. A raeeting:of the above was held in the Bewsey-rd ,V 7 es- leyan Church on Friday night, when the chair was occu- pied by the Rev.J.Kirtlanoupported,by the Rev.J.Yonge. There was only a small attendance. At the commence- ment the Rev. J. Yonge moved and the Rev. W. J. Kirk- land seconded that toe meeting of the Free Evangelical Church Council for Warrington and district heartily . approves of the Bill introduced into the Uouse of Commons by Mr. J. Carvell Williams, M.P., for the amendment of the Burial L ivrs and requests, the pre- sident and officers of the Council to sign and forward a petition to Parliament in support thereof." The same gentlement also moved tha.: the house to house visita- tion be referred to the Executive Committee. This was seconded and carried. The Rev. J. KikTLAN Lad great pleasure in introduc- ing the Rev. Dr. Mackennal who wanted to impress upon them all that eveniag that the object in the Free Church Councils was primarily, secondarily, and right through a religious object, an object in which they all had the same concern and which he was , very confident was dear to the hearts of them ' all. It:was a,reinarkable thing that that movement to- wards federation should have assumed in so short a time so great a prominence and have got into such activity and promise. There were considerably over 100 Free Church Councils in England, and tha t this had been accomplished in about two years was remarkable. They recognised that the free cnurches of this country were far in excess of other denominational formations. Nonconformity in the country had assumed the dimensions of a national Church doctrine, and he rejoiced in the philanthropic work which the Church Councils were giving themselves. Miss B. Durrois spoke in favour of the Executive Committee considering the desirabi.itv of having some , arrangements for a district nurse to work under the I Free Church Councils for Warrington, and cited the good done at different places which had come under her notice. The Rev. J. YONOS spoke of the beneficial work of the Free Church Councils and spoke of the plans and ideas to be carried out in connection with the district visitation. Votes of thanks to the Rev. Dr. Mackennal to the Wesleyan ministers were passed for lending the Bewsey- road Church for the meeting.</p>
